# Phase 212 (D-04, D-10): code-owner review on the check, the engine pin and the trust list.
#
# These paths define what the PR check runs (/.github/), which engine it trusts (the pin
# .okf/engine.lock) and who may approve a trusted-review sign-off (.okf/maintainers), all under
# /.okf/. A change to any of them needs a code owner's review.
#
# Set up once: replace the owner token @OKF_MAINTAINERS with this repository's maintainer team
# or user, then turn on "Require review from Code Owners" in the branch ruleset for the default
# branch (see the CI runbook). Until both are done this file protects nothing.
#
# Phase 219: .okf/publish.toml (the publish target and the minimum engine) is under /.okf/ too,
# so retargeting a publish needs a code owner's review.
/.github/ @OKF_MAINTAINERS
/.okf/ @OKF_MAINTAINERS
#
# Phase 214 (D-07, D-09): the rules skill grants nothing, but it steers the agent, and the scripts change
# repository settings (bootstrap, doctor, seeding). A change to either needs a code owner's review.
/.claude/ @OKF_MAINTAINERS
/scripts/ @OKF_MAINTAINERS
